("SL-C02","Write and issue environmental permits as the regulatory authority","Derive permit limits and conditions from statute, rules and technical analysis (e.g. NPDES effluent limits linked to TMDLs); draft fact sheets and deficiency letters; respond to comments; issue or deny; defend the record.","SC","DC","water|air|waste|wetlands","state|local|federal|tribal","transforming","AI|policy-reform","E","SL-079|SL-073|SL-076|SL-050","6.1.3|6.4.4|1.2.4","v1 6.1.3 and stage S3 are written from the applicant side ('securing regulatory authorization'). State postings describe the permit-writer side, a different task bundle with different AI exposure (drafting is compressible; limit derivation and defensibility are not).","SL"),
